# ---- Option A: open-source models (recommended, free) ---------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works. Text notes use LLM_MODEL, photos use VLM_MODEL.

# A1) Local with Ollama (fully offline; run the app with `npm run dev` on the same machine)
#     ollama pull qwen3-vl:4b-instruct      # 3.3 GB, reads text AND photos
#     (smaller laptop: qwen3-vl:2b-instruct, 1.9 GB)
LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
LLM_MODEL=qwen3-vl:4b-instruct
VLM_MODEL=qwen3-vl:4b-instruct
LLM_API_KEY=ollama

# A2) Hosted open-weight models for the Vercel deployment (Groq free tier, no card)
#     Check current model IDs at https://console.groq.com/docs/models
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=gsk_...
# LLM_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant
# VLM_MODEL=<a Groq model with image input>

# ---- Option B: Claude (paid) – only used when LLM_BASE_URL is NOT set -------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# With nothing set, the app uses the built-in rule-based extractor (no photo understanding).
